{"title":"Newton","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>You may be looking for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isaac_Newton\" title=\"Isaac Newton\">Isaac Newton</a> instead.</i></dd></dl>\n<p>A <b>Newton</b> (abbreviated N) is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Syst%C3%A8me_international\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Système international\">metric</a> measure of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Force\" title=\"Force\">force</a>, named for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isaac_Newton\" title=\"Isaac Newton\">Isaac Newton</a>, who did extensive research in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Physics\" title=\"Physics\">physics</a>, including his famous three laws of Physics.\n</p><p>One Newton is equal to one <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kilogram\" title=\"Kilogram\">kilogram</a> times one <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Meter\" title=\"Meter\">meter</a> per <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Second\" title=\"Second\">second</a> squared, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a598ba18e2e8ac3e00ff6fc98901fc8a2f48717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{N}=\\mathrm{kg}\\times \\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{s}^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"96\" height=\"33\" />. This is because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8c64c613e2d679f2491390f08dc20d998be2482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F = ma$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />, which means force (Newtons) equals mass (kilograms) times acceleration (meters per second squared).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Newton&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isaac_Newton\" title=\"Isaac Newton\">Isaac Newton</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Joule\" title=\"Joule\">Joule</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Watt\" title=\"Watt\">Watt</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Newton&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017120933\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 27/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 259/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 379/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.420      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.420      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5942:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017120933 and revision id 244168. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}